notes               = "Untitled in source. تعبیر کردن is specifically what you do to a dream — interpret it — so the winter dreams are to be read out in the willow's spring roots, not merely survived. میخواهم is printed without the zero-width joiner; kept as printed. The poem refuses the obvious role: not the wind that shakes the tree but the shepherd's fire beside it. 15 Bahman = 4 February 2004. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

بید باش...
میخواهم چون جویبار
در پای تو زمزمه کنم...
سبز بمان
تا همهٔ خواب‌های زمستانی‌ام را
در ریشه‌های بهاری تو تعبیر کنم...
بر تو می‌وَزَم...
آنسان که نسیم بی‌قرار می‌وَزَد...
بید باش...
من باد نیستم که تو را بلرزانم...
من آن آتشم که چوپانی عاشق روشن می‌کند....
بید باش...
تا برّه‌های خیالم...
در سایهٔ تو بخواب روند...
سبز بمان...
تا خواب‌های زمستانیم را...
در بهار تو تعبیر کنم...
۱۳۸۲/۱۱/۱۵

===machine===

Be a willow...
I want, like a brook,
to murmur at your feet...
Stay green
so that all my winter dreams
I may read out in your spring roots...
I blow upon you...
the way the restless breeze blows...
Be a willow...
I am not the wind, to set you shaking...
I am that fire a shepherd in love kindles....
Be a willow...
so the lambs of my imagining...
may go to sleep in your shade...
Stay green...
so that my winter dreams...
I may read out in your spring...
1382/11/15

===lantern===

Be a willow.
I want to murmur at your feet like a brook.
Stay green,
so that all my winter dreams
I may read out in your spring roots.
I blow upon you
the way the restless breeze blows.
Be a willow.
I am not the wind, to set you shaking.
I am that fire a shepherd in love kindles.
Be a willow,
so the lambs of my imagining
may go to sleep in your shade.
Stay green,
so that my winter dreams
I may read out in your spring...

1382/11/15

===translation===

===footnotes===

تعبیر is the word for interpreting a dream, and it governs both times the poem asks the
willow to stay green. The winter dreams are not to be endured until spring; spring is the thing
that will explain them.
